      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Missouri, Kansas, and Texas Railroad depot finished in 1871, and Louisburg’s first school opened the same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisburg%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2005 the historic Little Round House was moved to Louisburg City Lake, where the community restored it for its heritage value.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisburg%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A scenic byway traces a road built 1838‑1844 that carried soldiers and supplies between Fort Leavenworth, Fort Scott, and Fort Gibson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisburg%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Louisburg was incorporated as a third‑class city on November 3 1882, holding its first election just two weeks later on November 17.",
